<title>FRANCE: Bouygues soars on STET telcom deal.</title>
<headline>Bouygues soars on STET telcom deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French building company Bouygues opened sharply higher on the back of its announcement of a telecoms alliance with Italy's STET on Thursday evening.</p>
<p>At 0805 GMT, Bouygues was 3.4 percent higher at 504 francs.</p>
<p>STET will pay some 1.71 billion francs in 1996 and 1997 to obtain a stake in the Bouygues Decaux Telecom joint venture which aims to compete with France Telecom after liberalisation of the sector in 1998.</p>
<p>STET also joins a Bouygues-STET joint venture which, with Veba of Germany, will bid next week to run the telecoms network of French railway operator SNCF.</p>
</text>
